[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human epithelial (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=7,727): skew = 1.005, excess kurtosis = 2.000, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.83e-279, Jarque-Bera p = 0
  Normality of residuals: skew = 0.714, excess kurtosis = 1.700, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.46e-182, Jarque-Bera p = 0
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 353.484, p = 8.59e-43
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 109.167, p = 1.79e-47
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
